@startuml
scale 1 as 150 pixels

binary "DAT line" as DAT
binary "Stop At Block Gap Request\n(Control)" as SABGR
binary "Continue Request\n(Control)" as CR
binary "Write Transfer Active\n(Status)" as WTA
binary "DAT Line Active\n(Status)" as DLA
binary "Block Gap Event\n(Interrupt)" as BGE
binary "Transfer Complete\n(Interrupt)" as TC

@0
DAT is high
SABGR is low
CR is low
WTA is high
DLA is high
BGE is low
TC is low

@100
DAT is low
note bottom of DAT : Not last block

@150
SABGR is high

@200
DAT is high

@300
DAT is low
note bottom of DAT : Data block

@400
DAT is high
note bottom of DAT : CRC Status

@450
DAT is low
note bottom of DAT : Busy

@500
DAT is high

@550
WTA is low
BGE is high

@600
BGE is low
DLA is low
TC is high

@650
TC is low
SABGR is low

@700

legend right
  **Notation of the DAT line for write cycle**
  |= Phase |= Description |
  | Data block | Data transmission |
  | CRC Status | CRC check |
  | Busy | Card busy state |
  
  **Figure 3-30: Wait Write Transfer by Stop At Block Gap Request**
  
  **Conditions for accepting Stop At Block Gap Request:**
  (1) It is at the block gap
  (2) No valid write data remains in the Host Controller
  
  **After accepting Stop At Block Gap Request:**
  (1) Clear Write Transfer Active, generate Block Gap Event
  (2) After busy released, clear DAT Line Active, generate Transfer Complete
  (3) After accepting Transfer Complete, clear Stop At Block Gap Request
endlegend

@enduml